🎯 Important Logic to Remember
Add only if the item doesn't exist
if name in item:
    print("Item already exists!")
else:
    item[name] = qty
Increase stock
item[name] += qty0
Decrease stock only when enough is available
if qty0 <= item[name]:
    item[name] -= qty0
else:
    print("Not enough stock!")
Find low-stock items
for n in item:
    if item[n] < 5:
        print(n, item[n])

🧒 Simple memory trick

Think of the inventory as a shop notebook:

Add: Write a new item.
Restock: Increase its quantity.
Sell: Decrease its quantity, but never below zero.
View: Read the notebook.
Low stock: Find items with fewer than 5 units.


